landing-page/
# benchmarks/* not benchmarks/ — git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a `!` exception under `benchmarks/` never takes effect and new
# files in the published evidence pack cannot be added without -f.
#
# Un-ignoring the DIRECTORY is enough: `benchmarks/*` only matches its direct
# children, so everything below `benchmarks/longmemeval/` is trackable once git
# descends into it. Do not add a recursive `!benchmarks/longmemeval/**` — a
# later negation wins, so it would override the global `.env` and `data/` rules
# above for this whole subtree, in a public repo, in the one directory
# REPRODUCE.md tells people to download a dataset into.
benchmarks/*
!benchmarks/longmemeval/
!benchmarks/token/
experiments/
.archive/
MIGRATION.md
Dockerfile.test

# === Internal docs (not for public repo) ===
docs/archive/
docs/internal/
docs/guides/

