# === Maintainer-local development tooling — never committed ===
# Every pattern here is root-anchored (leading `/`). `intent/`, `evals/` and
# `sdlc/` without one would match ANY directory of that name at any depth —
# `intent` is already a product term (scripts/hooks/user-prompt-intent.js),
# `benchmarks/longmemeval/` shows nested data dirs are a real shape (so
# `benchmarks/<x>/evals/` is a plausible future path), and the product installs
# hooks into `.claude/` (a `tests/fixtures/.claude/` fixture would silently
# vanish from `git status` and from the tree `.verify/receipt.json` binds to).
# `.verify/` and `.sdlc-run/` are anchored too even though nothing creates them
# below the repo root today — verified against every file that touches either
# name (`git grep`); same failure mode as `intent/`, just not yet exercised.
#
# The five workflow files below are named explicitly, not by the glob
# `/.github/workflows/sdlc-*.yml` this block used to carry. That glob would
# also swallow a future PUBLIC workflow that happens to start with `sdlc-`
# (e.g. a checked-in `sdlc-verify.yml`) — silently, from both `git status`
# and the tree `treeHash()`/`.verify/receipt.json` bind to. Naming exactly
# the five that left keeps the ignore rule bounded to what actually left.
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.local.md
/scripts/sdlc/
/sdlc/
/evals/
/intent/
/docs/sdlc/
/docs/specs/
/docs/plans/
/REVIEW.md
/.github/workflows/sdlc-evals.yml
/.github/workflows/sdlc-loop.yml
/.github/workflows/sdlc-monitor.yml
/.github/workflows/sdlc-release.yml
/.github/workflows/sdlc-review.yml
/.verify/
/.sdlc-run/
